From 173a94861d7ee54068a88d34daa049b1051cb48b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Ang <hello@benjaminang.tv>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:04:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix: 1.4.1 candidate - lost answers (pytest captured
 logs, saturated rg), opt-in short-gap inlining, secrets screen

Code written by the local model (Qwen3.8 27B Kearuga ThinkingCap, xhigh), reviewed
and tested here; mechanical review fixes noted below.

- agent_formats: collapse long pytest Captured log/stdout/stderr sections (keep
  first/last 2, error-fingerprint and WARNING+ lines) instead of keeping them
  whole, so a failure block with a 60-line captured log no longer fails open.
- agent_formats: grep/rg saturation mode (query hits >= 80% of matches): keep
  definitions/assignments, other query words and distinct lines per file.
- compress_context/format_adapters: InliningGapMarker + compress_context
  inline_short_gaps=False: inline a dropped span when the marker is not shorter.
  Default path byte-identical (battery 15/15, sweep unchanged).
- secrets screen: AIza, sk_live_/rk_live_, bearer tokens, unquoted KEY=value.
- tests: new test files for all of the above; the Python-3.12+-dependent
  deep-malformed cache test accepts either sweep outcome (no raise, no retrieval).

Review fixes by hand: regex constants moved next to the pytest regexes, grep
regexes hoisted to module level, a dropped comment restored, the model's
sweep_ccr_cache change reverted (it broke 4 privacy/cleanup tests; docstring
corrected instead), test fixture text for the inline test and one assertion
in the captured-section test corrected.
